  "grammar_explanations": [
    {
      "slug": "past simple: irregular verbs (go, have, see)",
      "title_form": "Pasado simple: verbos irregulares (go, have, see)",
      "title_target": "Past simple: irregular verbs (go, have, see)",
      "description_md_form": "En inglés, algunos verbos no siguen la regla de agregar **-ed** para formar el pasado. Son los **verbos irregulares**. En esta lección vemos tres muy comunes:\n\n- **go** → **went** (ir)\n- **have** → **had** (tener)\n- **see** → **saw** (ver)\n\nLa forma es la misma para todas las personas: *I went*, *you went*, *he went*, *we went*, *they went*. No cambia.\n\nUsamos el pasado simple para contar **historias** y acciones terminadas en el pasado. Por ejemplo: *In my childhood, I went to the beach every summer.* (En mi infancia, iba a la playa cada verano).\n\nPara negar, usamos **didn't** + el verbo en forma base: *I didn't go*. Para preguntar, usamos **Did** + sujeto + verbo base: *Did you see it?*",
      "description_md_target": "In English, some verbs do not follow the rule of adding **-ed** to form the past. These are **irregular verbs**. In this lesson we see three very common ones:\n\n- **go** → **went**\n- **have** → **had**\n- **see** → **saw**\n\nThe form is the same for all persons: *I went*, *you went*, *he went*, *we went*, *they went*. It does not change.\n\nWe use the past simple to tell **stories** and finished actions in the past. For example: *In my childhood, I went to the beach every summer.*\n\nFor negatives, we use **didn't** + the base form: *I didn't go*. For questions, we use **Did** + subject + base verb: *Did you see it?*",
      "grammar_structure": "Subject + irregular past verb (went / had / saw) + complement",
      "conjugation_table": {
        "name": "past_simple_irregular",
        "headers": [
          "Verbo base",
          "Pasado simple",
          "Significado"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "go",
            "went",
            "ir"
          ],
          [
            "have",
            "had",
            "tener"
          ],
          [
            "see",
            "saw",
            "ver"
          ]
        ]
      },
